##############Instructions for computational reproducibility##############\
To computationally reproduce the results reported in the manuscript, you should follow the following steps:\
\
1. Open \'93osf_materials_reproducibility_check.Rproj\'94 in R Studio.\
2. Execute renv::restore() in the console (this will install required packages in the same version as listed above).\
3. Run the analysis_[experiment index].R scripts to reproduce the analyses reported in the main manuscript and the supplement.\
4. Run the visualization_[experiment index].R scripts to create the figures included in the main manuscript and the supplement.\
5. If needed, you can also run the cleaning_[experiment index].R scripts to re-create the cleaned data files using the raw/primary data in the data_raw_primary folder.\
